entry: what the studio can take from the todo (design/todo), its first
whole case: a tree of files a person runs, read by one verb and drawn by
two views. open, ranked by what each buys for what it costs.

the test it gives: an idea is a node, a lens or a verb
  node   a file or a folder: where an idea comes in, and where it is typed
  lens   a view made from nodes: the page, the walk, a tally, next. never
         edited, and never read back
  verb   what changes nodes: ed types a state, a rename reorders
  anything that is none of these is the wrong shape: a second list, a
  table of pointers, a store of its own, a page language between the tree
  and a view, a made file left inside the data.

1  next is a pronoun
   c is what you look at and m is where you have been; next is what you
   are for: the first leaf of the walk neither done nor blocked. todo -n
   prints its path, one line, so e `{todo -n} opens it and c `{todo -n}
   turns every lens to it. a few lines in medium/page/todo, and then the
   studio opens on the work, not on a folder.

2  fm draws the state
   fm says a thing's facts beside it (`fm/1-fs/22-facts.go`): its size,
   its age, a link's target. a state: from a text's head is one more
   fact, and then fm on a todo folder is the terminal's view of the todo
   page: one tree, two views, the goal of design/studio met first on the
   todo. the cost is a read of each file's first lines, the read the facts
   were built to avoid; take it only in a folder named todo.

3  a rename reorders
   a number is the order in a todo and in a tangle tree alike, so one verb
   serves both: put a node at place n, and renumber its siblings. making a
   thing 01 should be one key, not five mv's.

4  the run lens is a todo the machine types
   todo and pipeline are one structure with two evaluators. a test run
   that writes a node per test, its state done or fail, is a todo folder,
   and the page, the walk and the tally draw it as they are: the run lens
   needs no picture of its own.

5  after: is the graph lens's first data
   typed, small and exact: siblings, and the edges between them. figure
   draws a note as its parts and the messages between them, and a list
   with its after: lines is such a note.

6  nothing reads a lens
   the bug that showed it: a made outline left in the folder came back as
   a node, and a card's tally was read from a page that was made from the
   folders right beside it. a lens reads the thing, never another lens;
   worth a sixth line in design/studio.

7  one top
   ideas come in at the top of one todo. a tree with an open list of its
   own, as sys has in todo/, joins the top by a link, and the list becomes
   its children. that asks the list's notes to be nodes: a file each, and
   a folder only with a README, which todo/studio is not yet.
